Ha! ;) Especially when you’re talking about the last person.

But knowing how to count isn’t just knowing numbers. It’s knowing what counts.

Who’s included? Who’s excluded? What’s the order? What counts as showing, knowing, or recognizing something? And does the observer count themselves?

You can understand the entire pattern and still get the answer wrong because you counted the wrong things.

First know what you’re counting. Then know who’s doing the counting. And don’t forget to count yourself.

Sometimes the simplest arithmetic catches what the cleverest interpretation misses. ;)